data: {"type":"thread.item.done","item":{"created_at":"2026-01-27T05:38:21.943Z","id":"cti_cc593e96c2dc6f6120a7525a860737a7554366dd96ae269e","object":"chatkit.thread_item","type":"chatkit.widget","thread_id":"cthr_69783cc3804c8197943d7f864fc75d760c6c23afef15d171","widget":{"name":"Quiz_Widget","props":{"completed":false,"current_question_index":0,"current_retry_count":0,"disable_choices":true,"is_correct":false,"questions":[{"choices":[{"disabled":false,"label":"Thinking about thinking","value":"0"},{"disabled":false,"label":"Knowing about knowledge","value":"1"},{"disabled":true,"label":"Learning about learning","value":"2"},{"disabled":false,"label":"Controlling emotions","value":"3"}],"correct_choice_index":"0","explanation":"Metacognition is often described as thinking about thinking, which involves an awareness and understanding of one's own thought processes.","hints":["It's a common way to describe reflection on your thoughts.","It involves awareness of your own thinking.","It is often linked to self-regulation and learning."],"question_text":"What is metacognition often described as?"},{"choices":[{"disabled":false,"label":"Ignoring your inner voice","value":"0"},{"disabled":false,"label":"Taking conscious control of your inner voice","value":"1"},{"disabled":false,"label":"Listening only to external feedback","value":"2"},{"disabled":false,"label":"Avoiding thinking about your understanding","value":"3"}],"correct_choice_index":"1","explanation":"To employ metacognition in reading, one needs to take conscious control of their inner voice to assess and regulate understanding.","hints":["Focus on controlling your internal dialogue.","Metacognition involves deliberate awareness and regulation.","It is about being actively reflective while engaging with content."],"question_text":"Which of the following is a key component of employing metacognition while reading?"},{"choices":[{"disabled":false,"label":"Because it helps us control physical actions","value":"0"},{"disabled":false,"label":"Because it enables us to think about our thinking and regulate it","value":"1"},{"disabled":false,"label":"Because it replaces the need for learning strategies","value":"2"},{"disabled":false,"label":"Because it focuses only on academic success","value":"3"}],"correct_choice_index":"1","explanation":"Metacognition is crucial in everyday life because it helps us think about our thinking, regulate our reasoning, and improve problem-solving and decision-making.","hints":["It involves reflection on thought processes.","Its importance extends beyond academics.","It helps in goal setting and critical thinking."],"question_text":"According to the article, why is metacognition important for everyday life?"},{"choices":[{"disabled":false,"label":"The story of Einstein's relativity","value":"0"},{"disabled":false,"label":"Houston, we have a problem! in Apollo 13","value":"1"},{"disabled":false,"label":"The Tower of Hanoi puzzle","value":"2"},{"disabled":false,"label":"The Turing Test for artificial intelligence","value":"3"}],"correct_choice_index":"1","explanation":"The article uses the story of 'Houston, we have a problem!' from Apollo 13 as a thought experiment demonstrating decision-making and problem-solving, which relates to metacognitive strategies.","hints":["It's a historical NASA story.","It's related to space mission problem-solving.","It illustrates decision-making processes in crises."],"question_text":"What example does the article give of a thought experiment related to metacognition?"}],"show_feedback":true,"total":4}}}}
